From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:19:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] hjviewer: E2E: a refusal for access at a session's
 start shows the app's box

The screen and stream commands printed hbbs's refusal as it came and
ended with exit code 5, while the app (and the E2E's port forwarding)
shows its own text in its place through
Interface::on_establish_connection_error. They now take the same path,
so the E2E sees the box a user sees: the app's A1 or A2, then
'access refused' and exit code 5. A build without the account part
ends as before.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UGRoRVHEhxg8GAbP842qdV
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hjviewer_e2e.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hjviewer_e2e.rs b/src/hjviewer_e2e.rs
index f412d72..3a6d3bf 100644
--- a/src/hjviewer_e2e.rs
+++ b/src/hjviewer_e2e.rs
@@ -230,6 +230,10 @@ async fn desktop(id: String, password: String, watch: Watch) -> i32 {
             Ok(res) => res,
             Err(err) => {
                 eprintln!("hjv-e2e: {err}");
+                if crate::hjviewer_access::refusal_text(&err.to_string()).is_some() {
+                    // the app's box in place of hbbs's text, as port forwarding shows it (exit 5)
+                    interface.on_establish_connection_error(err.to_string());
+                }
                 return if crate::hjviewer_access::is_refusal(&err.to_string()) {
                     5
                 } else {
